From 9fa742720586c45595df95fac3c12d992d59a8ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: darkmaniac7 <31073889+darkmaniac7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:08:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] firmware: lab knobs (fast subsets, reset lead, dither,
 hold at release, rail_code)

On one card on 2026-11-20 the fast subsets ran on push2, and the dither
and the post-train SCL hold on push1; a hold that starts at the
release has not been run. With fast 0/1, t_restore above
-1000, revert 0/1 and hold 0 the timeline is unchanged.

- fast 2..7: one subset of the fast profile (2 = 0x30+0x32, 3 = 0x30,
  4 = 0x32, 5 = 0xBA, 6 = 0xB9, 7 = 0x45); the card's six values are
  captured and restored as before. fast outside 0..7 aborts instead of
  meaning "full fast".
- t_restore <= -1000 (down to -20000): the PEX_RST assert, the 600 mV
  setup and the two setup writes move to t_restore, so a long dip that
  starts before -1000 is not overwritten. A WARN line flags any VOUT step
  before the setup write.
- revert=2: one-VID dither. Odd pulses are mv_to_code(v_dip) + 1 (one VID
  code, 6.25 mV, shallower), with no restore and no gap inside the train
  and no hand-back.
- hold_ms > 0 with the train finished before t = 0: SCL is held from
  t = 0 and the stock restore waits for the hold (t_revert still counts).
  Trains that write after t = 0 keep the old post-train hold.
- After the shot: READ_VOUT, and only if it reads below 500 or fails, the
  seven status bytes before the CML read, printed as
  rail_code=<n> status 7a=.. 7b=.. 7c=.. 7d=.. 7f=.. 80=.. 78=..
  This is one extra PMBus read per shot at default parameters.
- The echo adds reset_at, dither and hold_at; pw and gap there are the
  resolved values (the 36 us floor stays).

A host-side simulation of glitch_cmd gives the same PMBus writes and
assert times as the timing build for default commands. Builds for pico2_w
(RP2350A and RP2350B) and pico2, normal and debug, with no warnings.
